      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T00:57:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "naming nit. The \"maybe\" pattern isn\u0027t terrible, but I think we have other (better) options here:\n\n1) succinctrly stating the condition, like startVcnIfInactiveLocked()\n2) Or, better, just add the necessary line of code to check and see if there\u0027s a VCN instance. That also avoids a \"maybe\" function and makes it super clear what\u0027s happening.\n\nBoth avoid anybody having to go to the maybe() function to know what conditions will cause this, and then the formerly-maybe function can unconditionally do something. The reason to keep the condition in the maybe() function is if that condition will need to be checked every time the thing needs to happen AND it will be done in multiple places.",
      "range": {
